  "calendar": "julian",
  "register": "documentary, and wary of the coherent league",
  "summary": "The Hanse moved wax, furs, grain, cloth, salt, and stockfish through fenced compounds at Novgorod, Bergen, Bruges, and London, held together not by a treasury or a navy but by privileges renewed town by town, correspondence carried by whoever happened to be travelling, and the threat of collective boycott. Lübeck convened the assemblies without ever ruling them, and the network's coherence rose and fell with how many towns found a given quarrel worth their own money. It did not collapse in 1669: the last general diet, attended by nine towns, delegated its unfinished business to Lübeck, Hamburg, and Bremen rather than dissolving anything.",
