    {
      "name": "The Teutonic Order",
      "ntype": "agent",
      "lat": 54.0397,
      "lng": 19.0274,
      "born": 1241,
      "born_confidence": "approximate",
      "died": 1466,
      "died_confidence": "approximate",
      "region": "State of the Teutonic Order in Prussia and Livonia",
      "note": "Regulator and sometime patron of the Prussian and Livonian trading towns, and beneficiary of the Northern Crusades that subordinated the populations underlying the network's eastern commodities. Its defeat at Tannenberg in 1410 disrupted eastern finance and trade; the Second Peace of Thorn in 1466 transferred Royal Prussia, including Danzig, to the Polish crown.",
      "sources": [
